---
import Callout from "../../components/Callout.astro";
import PageShell from "../../components/PageShell.astro";
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="AI Tool Config Files - AI Training Guide">
	<PageShell chapterId="fundamentals" subChapterId="ai-tool-config-files">
		<div class="prose space-y-6">
			<p>
				Every AI coding tool has its own set of configuration files that control how it behaves in
				your project. These files tell the AI about your coding standards, project structure, and
				workflows. Understanding where each tool keeps its files is practical knowledge you'll use
				constantly, especially if your team uses more than one tool.
			</p>

			<Callout variant="info" title="Using multiple tools?">
				<p>
					If your team uses several AI tools (common in organizations), you may want to symlink
					shared instruction files rather than duplicating content. For example, you could maintain
					one canonical rules file and symlink it to each tool's expected location. GitHub Copilot's
					coding agent actually reads <code>CLAUDE.md</code> and <code>AGENTS.md</code> files
					automatically, which reduces duplication across those tools.
				</p>
			</Callout>

			<h3>Project Instructions / Rules</h3>

			<p>
				These are the files where you describe your project to the AI: coding conventions, tech
				stack, do's and don'ts. Every tool has its own version of this concept.
			</p>

			<div class="my-8 overflow-x-auto">
				<table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
					<thead>
						<tr class="border-b-2 border-stone-300">
							<th class="text-left py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">File / Location</th>
							<th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-semibold text-stone-700">Claude Code</th>
							<th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-semibold text-stone-700">Codex</th>
							<th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-semibold text-stone-700">Antigravity CLI</th>
							<th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-semibold text-stone-700">Copilot</th>
							<th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-semibold text-stone-700">Cursor</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
							<td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">CLAUDE.md</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-green-600 font-bold">&#10003;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span
									class="text-amber-500 cursor-help"
									title="Copilot's coding agent reads this file when present"
									>&#10003;*</span
								>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr class="border-b border-stone-200 bg-stone-50/50">
							<td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">AGENTS.md</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-green-600 font-bold">&#10003;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-green-600 font-bold">&#10003;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span
									class="text-amber-500 cursor-help"
									title="Copilot's coding agent reads this file when present"
									>&#10003;*</span
								>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span
									class="text-amber-500 cursor-help"
									title="Cursor reads AGENTS.md at root or nested in subdirectories"
									>&#10003;*</span
								>
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr class="border-b border-stone-200 bg-stone-50/50">
							<td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">.github/copilot-instructions.md</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-green-600 font-bold">&#10003;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
							<td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">.cursor/rules/*.mdc</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-green-600 font-bold">&#10003;</span>
							</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>

			<p class="text-xs text-stone-500 -mt-4">
				<span class="text-amber-500 font-bold">&#10003;*</span> = also reads this file when present,
				in addition to its own native instruction files. Hover for details.
			</p>

			<h3>Skills & Reusable Workflows</h3>

			<p>
				Skills are packaged, reusable workflows that an AI tool can invoke on demand, like
				"write a commit message" or "break down a ticket." There is now an{" "}
				<a
					href="https://agentskills.io"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					class="font-semibold">open standard called Agent Skills</a
				>{" "}that most tools have adopted. A widely-adopted convention is{" "}
				<code>.agents/skills/&lt;name&gt;/SKILL.md</code>, and most tools search this location, though each tool also uses its own
				legacy paths.
			</p>

			<div class="my-8 overflow-x-auto">
				<table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
					<thead>
						<tr class="border-b-2 border-stone-300">
							<th class="text-left py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Tool</th>
							<th class="text-left py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">
								Project Skills Paths
							</th>
							<th class="text-left py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">
								User Skills Paths
							</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
							<td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Claude Code</td>
							<td class="py-3 px-3">
								<span class="font-mono text-xs block">.claude/skills/</span>
								<span
									class="text-[11px] text-stone-400 cursor-help"
									title="Also searches nested directories: packages/frontend/.claude/skills/ etc. Legacy .claude/commands/ also supported."
									>also nested dirs, legacy commands/</span
								>
							</td>
							<td class="py-3 px-3">
								<span class="font-mono text-xs">~/.claude/skills/</span>
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr class="border-b border-stone-200 bg-stone-50/50">
							<td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Codex</td>
							<td class="py-3 px-3">
								<span class="font-mono text-xs block">.agents/skills/</span>
								<span
									class="text-[11px] text-stone-400 cursor-help"
									title="Searches upward: .agents/skills/, ../.agents/skills/, up to $REPO_ROOT/.agents/skills/."
									>searches up to repo root</span
								>
							</td>
							<td class="py-3 px-3">
								<span class="font-mono text-xs block">~/.agents/skills/</span>
								<span
									class="text-[11px] text-stone-400 cursor-help"
									title="Also checks /etc/codex/skills/ for admin-level skills"
									>also /etc/codex/skills/</span
								>
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
							<td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Antigravity CLI</td>
							<td class="py-3 px-3">
								<span class="font-mono text-xs block">.agents/skills/</span>
								<span
									class="text-[11px] text-stone-400 cursor-help"
									title="Each skill is a directory containing a SKILL.md file, per the Agent Skills standard."
									>Agent Skills standard</span
								>
							</td>
							<td class="py-3 px-3">
								<span class="text-xs text-stone-400">not yet documented</span>
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr class="border-b border-stone-200 bg-stone-50/50">
							<td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Copilot</td>
							<td class="py-3 px-3">
								<span class="font-mono text-xs block">.github/skills/</span>
								<span
									class="text-[11px] text-stone-400 cursor-help"
									title="Also searches .claude/skills/ for compatibility. Prompt files (.github/prompts/*.prompt.md) are a separate Copilot-specific feature for reusable chat prompts."
									>also .claude/skills/, prompts/</span
								>
							</td>
							<td class="py-3 px-3">
								<span class="font-mono text-xs block">~/.copilot/skills/</span>
								<span
									class="text-[11px] text-stone-400 cursor-help"
									title="Also checks ~/.agents/skills/"
									>also ~/.agents/skills/</span
								>
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
							<td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Cursor</td>
							<td class="py-3 px-3">
								<span class="font-mono text-xs block">.agents/skills/</span>
								<span
									class="text-[11px] text-stone-400 cursor-help"
									title="Also searches .cursor/skills/, .claude/skills/, and .codex/skills/ for compatibility"
									>also .cursor/, .claude/, .codex/skills/</span
								>
							</td>
							<td class="py-3 px-3">
								<span class="font-mono text-xs block">~/.cursor/skills/</span>
								<span
									class="text-[11px] text-stone-400 cursor-help"
									title="Also checks ~/.claude/skills/ and ~/.codex/skills/ for compatibility"
									>also ~/.agents/, ~/.claude/, ~/.codex/skills/</span
								>
							</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>

			<p class="text-xs text-stone-500 -mt-4">
				Hover over the gray text for details on additional search paths and compatibility.
			</p>

			<Callout variant="tip" title="The Agent Skills standard">
				<p>
					If you maintain skills that should work across multiple tools, use the widely-supported{" "}
					<code>.agents/skills/&lt;name&gt;/SKILL.md</code> path. Most tools now search this
					location in addition to their own. Each skill is a directory containing a{" "}
					<code>SKILL.md</code> file with YAML frontmatter (<code>name</code> and{" "}
					<code>description</code> required) plus optional <code>scripts/</code>,{" "}
					<code>references/</code>, and <code>assets/</code> subdirectories.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-2">
					For ready-made skills, <a href="https://skills.sh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-orange-600 underline hover:text-orange-700">skills.sh</a> is Vercel's public directory of installable agent skills (add one with <code>npx skills</code>).
				</p>
			</Callout>

			<h3>Custom Agents / Sub-agents</h3>

            <p>
                Some tools let you define specialized sub-agents that the AI can delegate specific tasks to. This is a more advanced feature that not all tools
                support yet. For more information, see the <strong>Sub-agents</strong> section in{" "}
                <a href="/development/additional-features" target="_self">
                    Additional Features
                </a>.
            </p>

            <div class="my-8 overflow-x-auto">
                <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
                    <thead>
                        <tr class="border-b-2 border-stone-300">
                            <th class="text-left py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Tool</th>
                            <th class="text-left py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700"> Project Agents Path </th>
                            <th class="text-left py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700"> User Agents Path </th>
                            <th class="text-left py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700"> Docs </th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Claude Code</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">.claude/agents/&lt;name&gt;.md</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">~/.claude/agents/&lt;name&gt;.md</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs"><a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents" target="_blank">Claude Sub-agents</a></td>

                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-stone-200 bg-stone-50/50">
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Codex</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">.codex/agents/&lt;name&gt;.toml</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">~/.codex/agents/&lt;name&gt;.toml</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs"><a href="https://developers.openai.com/codex/subagents" target="_blank">Codex Sub-agents</a></td>

                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Antigravity CLI</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs text-stone-400">not yet documented</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs text-stone-400">not yet documented</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs"><a href="https://antigravity.google/docs/cli-overview" target="_blank">Antigravity CLI docs</a></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-stone-200 bg-stone-50/50">
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Copilot</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">.github/agents/&lt;name&gt;.agent.md</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">~/.copilot/agents/&lt;name&gt;.agent.md</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs">
                                <span class="block">
                                    <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/copilot/customization/custom-agents" target="_blank">Copilot Custom Agents</a>
                                </span>
                                <span>
                                    <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/copilot/agents/subagents" target="_blank">Copilot Sub-agents</a>
                                </span>
                            </td>

                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Cursor</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">.cursor/agents/&lt;name&gt;.md</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">~/.cursor/agents/&lt;name&gt;.md</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs"><a href="https://cursor.com/docs/subagents" target="_blank">Cursor Sub-agents</a></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <h3>Hooks</h3>

            <p>
                Hooks let you run shell commands automatically in response to tool events. They are configured in the tool's settings file, not in
                instruction files like <code>CLAUDE.md</code>. Support varies significantly across tools. For more information, see the <strong>Hooks</strong>{" "}
                section in <a href="/development/additional-features" target="_self">Additional Features</a>.
            </p>

            <div class="my-8 overflow-x-auto">
                <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
                    <thead>
                        <tr class="border-b-2 border-stone-300">
                            <th class="text-left py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Tool</th>
                            <th class="text-left py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Project Config</th>
                            <th class="text-left py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">User Config</th>
                            <th class="text-left py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Docs</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Claude Code</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">
                                <span class='block'>.claude/settings.json or</span>
                                <span>.claude/settings.local.json</span>
                            </td>
                             <td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">~/.claude/settings.json</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs"><a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks" target="_blank">Claude Code Hooks</a></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-stone-200 bg-stone-50/50">
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Codex</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs">.codex/hooks.json</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-mono text-xs ">~/.codex/hooks.json</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs">
                                <a href="https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks" target="_blank">Codex Hooks</a>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Antigravity CLI</td>
                             <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs text-stone-400">not yet documented</td>
                             <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs">
                                <span class="text-stone-400">not yet documented</span>
                                
                            </td>

                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs">
                                <a href="https://antigravity.google/docs/cli-overview" target="_blank">Antigravity CLI docs</a>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-stone-200 bg-stone-50/50">
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Copilot</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs font-mono">.github/hooks/</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs text-stone-400">&mdash;</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs">
                                <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/cloud-agent/use-hooks" target="_blank">Copilot Hooks</a>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Cursor</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs font-mono">.cursor/hooks.json</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs font-mono">~/.cursor/hooks.json</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-3 text-xs">
                                <a href="https://cursor.com/docs/hooks" target="_blank">Cursor Hooks</a>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <h3>Directory-Scoped Rules & Skills</h3>

			<p>
				For monorepos and larger projects, some tools let you place rules and skills in
				subdirectories so they only apply when the AI is working in that part of the codebase.
			</p>

			<div class="my-8 overflow-x-auto">
				<table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
					<thead>
						<tr class="border-b-2 border-stone-300">
							<th class="text-left py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-stone-700">Feature</th>
							<th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-semibold text-stone-700">Claude Code</th>
							<th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-semibold text-stone-700">Codex</th>
							<th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-semibold text-stone-700">Antigravity CLI</th>
							<th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-semibold text-stone-700">Copilot</th>
							<th class="text-center py-3 px-2 font-semibold text-stone-700">Cursor</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
							<td class="py-3 px-3 text-stone-700">Subdirectory rules</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span
									class="text-green-600 font-bold cursor-help"
									title="Place CLAUDE.md in any subdirectory, e.g. src/CLAUDE.md"
									>&#10003;</span
								>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span
									class="text-green-600 font-bold cursor-help"
									title="Place AGENTS.md in any subdirectory, e.g. src/AGENTS.md"
									>&#10003;</span
								>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr class="border-b border-stone-200 bg-stone-50/50">
							<td class="py-3 px-3 text-stone-700">Path-scoped rules</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span
									class="text-green-600 font-bold cursor-help"
									title=".claude/rules/ directory with files scoped to paths"
									>&#10003;</span
								>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span
									class="text-green-600 font-bold cursor-help"
									title=".codex/rules/ directory"
									>&#10003;</span
								>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span class="text-stone-300">&mdash;</span>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span
									class="text-green-600 font-bold cursor-help"
									title=".github/instructions/*.instructions.md with applyTo glob patterns"
									>&#10003;</span
								>
							</td>
							<td class="text-center py-3 px-2">
								<span
									class="text-green-600 font-bold cursor-help"
